  "verified_against": {
    "source": "release-manifest.json",
    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.24.0 release assets and hashed independently. v5.24.0 removes the last engine-side literal that made a DARQ install differ in behaviour from a Pegasus one: the OpenCode notifier plugin compared the live session's agent against a hardcoded \"pegasus-orchestrator\", so in DARQ -- which renames its orchestrator -- the comparison never matched and the plugin never fired. The engine now ships the plugin with an {{orchestrator}} placeholder filled at install time from the content-declared name, and renders every bundled adapter asset through that vocabulary rather than special-casing one file. Only the `pegasus` artifact changed; install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.23.0."
  }
